--expect
7 64 0 0 17
--expect-why
DERIVED BY HAND from `pikegas.kin` plus the accounting stubs the driver's own
`-head` sections define. Nothing was read off a run.

  charge-compile rt n = (charge-work rt n; return n)
  charge-subject rt s = (let n = s-bytes rt s in charge-bytes rt n; return n)

and the fixture's `-head` supplies the three things kin delegates to:

  s-bytes v      = v            (the Value IS its byte count here)
  charge-work n  = steps += n
  charge-bytes n = charge-work (n / 8 + 1)

FIELDS 1-4 ARE THE RETURN VALUES, and the point of printing them is that the
two functions return DIFFERENT QUANTITIES from what they charge:

  a = charge-compile 7      -> 7    program words, and 7 is also what it charged
  b = charge-subject 64     -> 64   BYTES -- not the 9 steps it charged
  c = charge-compile 0      -> 0
  d = charge-subject 0      -> 0    bytes -- not the 1 step it charged

`b` is the one that can only be right. Kin says charge-subject answers the
subject's bytes, while the price it pays goes through `charge-bytes`, which
divides by 8 and adds one; a version that returned the amount charged would
print 9 here and 1 for `d`, and the whole line would still be self-consistent.

FIELD 5 IS THE RUNNING TOTAL, and it accumulates all four calls in order:

  charge-compile 7   charge-work 7            steps  0 -> 7
  charge-subject 64  charge-work (64/8 + 1)=9 steps  7 -> 16
  charge-compile 0   charge-work 0            steps 16 -> 16
  charge-subject 0   charge-work (0/8 + 1)=1  steps 16 -> 17

so 17. The third and fourth calls are the ones that say the charge happens
UNCONDITIONALLY, which is the divergence this source exists to close -- kin's
own doc says a compile is "CHARGED ON EVERY COMPILE, hit or miss". A
zero-word compile adds nothing (16 stays 16 -- a zero charge and a skipped
charge are indistinguishable there, which is exactly why the fourth call is
also in the line), and an EMPTY subject still costs 1, because
`charge-bytes`'s `+ 1` is a per-call floor. That last 1 is the whole of the
difference between 16 and 17: an implementation that took an empty subject as
free work, or that charged only on a miss, lands on 16.
